Ticket #4471 contains two separate problems. The export overlaps between pages, so the table
removes duplicate report IDs before it groups reports by tenant locale, booking form, and report
channel.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Shared parser

The shared parser reads every date month first. The affected tenants write the day first, so
valid local dates are interpreted with the month and day reversed.

## booking-v3 date hint

`booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` for tenants whose locales use day-first dates. Their users enter
what the hint asks for, but the form reads the value using the tenant locale. This is a separate
problem because it only occurs through `booking-v3` forms.

<Callout>
Keep one engineering ticket per cause. Intake tags are guesses; classify these reports from the
tenant locale, booking form, and channel.
</Callout>

